// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  core.prisma — BUI CORE DATA LAYER  ·  🔒 LOCKED FILE
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  AI coding agents must NEVER edit this file. It is protected by:
//    • AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md instructions
//    • opencode.json and .claude/settings.json edit-deny rules
//    • prisma/core.lock checksum, verified by scripts/schema-guard.mjs in
//      pre-commit and CI
//    • CODEOWNERS: any change requires the owner's review
//  Changes here are made by a human, reviewed, and the lock re-signed with
//  `node scripts/schema-guard.mjs --sign`.
//
//  What lives here: everything the platform depends on to be correct.
//    Master data ........ legal entities, employees + org structure, customers,
//                         suppliers, products/SKUs, tax rates, price lists
//    Sales cycle ........ enquiry → rates → estimate → sales order
//                         (stage machine with approval gates)
//    Operations ......... stock ledger, reservations, purchasing, dispatch
//    Finance + GST ...... invoices, credit/debit notes, receipts, supplier
//                         bills, double-entry ledger, e-invoice / e-way bill
//    Platform ........... roles & permissions, actions + escalation,
//                         approvals, notifications, integrations, domain events
//    Accountability ..... audit events, row-change log (DB triggers),
//                         access log (every record viewed)
//
//  Rules for everything outside this file (automation.prisma, legacy.prisma):
//    1. They may READ core ids and store them as plain columns
//       (`customerId String @db.Uuid`, no @relation). Prisma requires both sides
//       of a relation to be declared, so a relation into core would force an
//       edit here. Integrity of those soft references is checked by
//       DataQualityIssue sweeps.
//    2. Core never references automation or legacy models.
//    3. Runtime writes to core go through the core service layer, which
//       checks permissions, sets the actor for the audit triggers, and emits
//       a DomainEvent. Automation reacts to DomainEvents.
//
//  Conventions
//    • Postgres schema "core". UUID v7 primary keys (time-ordered).
//    • Money Decimal(18,2); unit prices Decimal(18,4); quantities
//      Decimal(18,3); tax rates Decimal(5,2).
//    • Timestamps timestamptz (UTC, shown in Asia/Kolkata). Pure dates @db.Date.
//    • No createdBy / updatedBy columns: the row-change trigger records the
//      actor of every INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE in RowChangeLog.
//    • Business documents carry a `version` for optimistic concurrency.
//    • Issued legal documents (invoices, notes, posted journals, stock
//      entries) are immutable; corrections are new documents (see
//      prisma/sql/core/001_core_platform.sql).
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
  schemas  = ["core", "automation", "public"]
}

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

